              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:9",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And it is according to the dignity of his office that he should preside over the council of the church; and it is his privilege to be assisted by two other presidents, appointed after the same manner that he himself was appointed.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:10",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And in case of the absence of one or both of those who are appointed to assist him, he has power to preside over the council without an assistant; and in case he himself is absent, the other presidents have power to preside in his stead, both or either of them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:11",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Whenever a high council of the church of Christ is regularly organized, according to the foregoing pattern, it shall be the duty of the twelve councilors to cast lots by numbers, and thereby ascertain who of the twelve shall speak first, commencing with number one and so in succession to number twelve.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:12",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Whenever this council convenes to act upon any case, the twelve councilors shall consider whether it is a difficult one or not; if it is not, two only of the councilors shall speak upon it, according to the form above written.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:13",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "But if it is thought to be difficult, four shall be appointed; and if more difficult, six; but in no case shall more than six be appointed to speak.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:14",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "The accused, in all cases, has a right to one-half of the council, to prevent insult or injustice.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 88,
            "end": 97,
            "text": "TG Injustice."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Injustice.",
            "prettyString": "TG Injustice",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Injustice",
                "entryId": "tg-injustice",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:15",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And the councilors appointed to speak before the council are to present the case, after the evidence is examined, in its true light before the council; and every man is to speak according to equity and justice.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 202,
            "end": 209,
            "text": "TG Justice."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Justice.",
            "prettyString": "TG Justice",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Justice",
                "entryId": "tg-justice",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:16",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "Those councilors who draw even numbers, that is, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, and 12, are the individuals who are to stand up in behalf of the accused, and prevent insult and injustice.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "BD Lots, casting of."
          },
          {
            "start": 162,
            "end": 171,
            "text": "TG Injustice."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "BD Lots, casting of.",
            "prettyString": "BD Lots, casting of",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "bd",
                "title": "Lots, casting of",
                "entryId": "bd-lots-casting-of",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "raw": "TG Injustice.",
            "prettyString": "TG Injustice",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Injustice",
                "entryId": "tg-injustice",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:17",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "In all cases the accuser and the accused shall have a privilege of speaking for themselves before the council, after the evidences are heard and the councilors who are appointed to speak on the case have finished their remarks.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 135,
            "end": 140,
            "text": "John 7:51; Acts 25:16."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "John 7:51; Acts 25:16.",
            "prettyString": "John 7:51; Acts 25:16",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "john",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 7,
                    "end": 7,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 51,
                        "end": 51
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "acts",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 25,
                    "end": 25,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 16,
                        "end": 16
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:18",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "After the evidences are heard, the councilors, accuser and accused have spoken, the president shall give a decision according to the understanding which he shall have of the case, and call upon the twelve councilors to sanction the same by their vote.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 219,
            "end": 227,
            "text": "TG Common Consent."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Common Consent.",
            "prettyString": "TG Common Consent",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Common Consent",
                "entryId": "tg-common-consent",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:19",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "But should the remaining councilors, who have not spoken, or any one of them, after hearing the evidences and pleadings impartially, discover an error in the decision of the president, they can manifest it, and the case shall have a re-hearing.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 145,
            "end": 150,
            "text": "Isa. 56:1."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Isa. 56:1.",
            "prettyString": "Isaiah 56:1",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "isaiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 56,
                    "end": 56,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 1,
                        "end": 1
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:20",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "And if, after a careful re-hearing, any additional light is shown upon the case, the decision shall be altered accordingly.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:21",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "But in case no additional light is given, the first decision shall stand, the majority of the council having power to determine the same.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:22",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "In case of difficulty respecting doctrine or principle, if there is not a sufficiency written to make the case clear to the minds of the council, the president may inquire and obtain the mind of the Lord by revelation.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "Num. 9:8."
          },
          {
            "start": 187,
            "end": 191,
            "text": "Lev. 24:12; D&C 68:4. TG Revelation."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Num. 9:8.",
            "prettyString": "Numbers 9:8",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "numbers",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 9,
                    "end": 9,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 8,
                        "end": 8
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:23",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "The high priests, when abroad, have power to call and organize a council after the manner of the foregoing, to settle difficulties, when the parties or either of them shall request it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:24",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "And the said council of high priests shall have power to appoint one of their own number to preside over such council for the time being.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:25",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "It shall be the duty of said council to transmit, immediately, a copy of their proceedings, with a full statement of the testimony accompanying their decision, to the high council of the seat of the First Presidency of the Church.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "TG Church Organization; Order."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Church Organization; Order.",
            "prettyString": "TG Church Organization; TG Order",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Church Organization",
                "entryId": "tg-church-organization",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              },
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Order",
                "entryId": "tg-order",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:26",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "Should the parties or either of them be dissatisfied with the decision of said council, they may appeal to the high council of the seat of the First Presidency of the Church, and have a re-hearing, which case shall there be conducted, according to the former pattern written, as though no such decision had been made.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:27",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "This council of high priests abroad is only to be called on the most difficult cases of church matters; and no common or ordinary case is to be sufficient to call such council.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 78,
            "text": "D&C 107:78."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "D&C 107:78.",
            "prettyString": "D&C 107:78",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "doctrineandcovenants",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 107,
                    "end": 107,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 78,
                        "end": 78
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:28",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "The traveling or located high priests abroad have power to say whether it is necessary to call such a council or not.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 102:29",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 102,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "There is a distinction between the high council or traveling high priests abroad, and the traveling high council composed of the twelve apostles, in their decisions.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "D&C 107:23–24, 31, 35–38."
          },
          {
            "start": 136,
            "end": 144,
            "text": "TG Apostles."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
